\qc\b Special Project 1: Quasi-One-Dimensional Nozzle Flow with Friction and Heat Addition\b0\par
\ql\line
\b Abstract\b0\line
This report evaluates the variation of Mach number, static temperature, and static pressure along a converging-diverging nozzle axis beginning at the throat, x = 0, using the Chapter 8 Shapiro formulation. A MATLAB implementation was developed to compare four required scenarios: (a) isentropic flow, (b) friction only, (c) heat addition only, and (d) combined friction and heat addition. The inlet total conditions were set to p0 = 50 MPa (gage) and T0 = 3000 K. Results are presented as three plots (Mach number, temperature, and semilog pressure) with all four scenarios overlaid for direct comparison.\line
\line
\b 1. Introduction\b0\line
Compressible flow through nozzles is highly sensitive to area change, wall friction, and heat transfer. Near the throat, M = 1 produces an indeterminate form in the differential equation for Mach number variation, requiring careful numerical handling and small spatial steps. The objective of this project is to compute and compare x-wise flow-property evolution for the four assigned physical cases and present clear engineering plots suitable for grading.\line
\line
\b 2. Governing Approach\b0\line
The nozzle geometry is read from a file and interpolated onto a fine x-grid. From the radius profile, area and logarithmic area derivatives are calculated. The mass flow rate is initialized from choked-flow conditions at the throat. For each case, the code computes local total-temperature variation (when heat addition is present), friction source terms (when wall friction is present), and integrates d(M^2)/dx using a robust branch function near M = 1.\line
\line
Static properties are then recovered from standard compressible-flow relations:\line
- T = T0 / [1 + (k-1)M^2/2]\line
- V = M\~a, with a = sqrt(kRT)\line
- rho = mdot/(AV)\line
- p = rhoRT\line
\line
\b 3. Input Parameters and Manipulated Variables\b0\line
\b Fixed assignment inputs\b0\line
- k = 1.4\line
- R = 287 J/(kg-K)\line
- Inlet total temperature: T0,in = 3000 K\line
- Inlet total pressure: p0 = 50 MPa (gage)\line
\line
\b Case-defining variables\b0\line
- Friction coefficient, f\line
- Heat-addition slope to total temperature, q\line
\line
\b Numerical control variables\b0\line
- Initial location near throat: x0\line
- Initial Mach slightly above 1: M0\line
- Spatial increment: dx (small for smooth curves)\line
- Adaptive step-halving near singular behavior at M = 1\line
\line
\b 4. Required Cases\b0\line
(a) Isentropic: f = 0, q = 0\line
(b) Friction only: f = 0.005, q = 0\line
(c) Heat transfer only: f = 0, q \~!= 0\line
(d) Friction + heat transfer: f = 0.005, q \~!= 0\line
